{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q247914","formula":"Co₃(AsO₄)₂·8H₂O","hill":"As2Co3H16O16","elements":["H","O","Co","As"],"composition":{"H":16.0,"O":16.0,"As":2.0,"Co":3.0},"names":{"en":"Erythrite","ru":"Эритрин","uk":"Еритрин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Erythrite, also known as red cobalt, previously cobalt ochre is a secondary hydrated cobalt arsenate mineral with the formula Co3(AsO4)2•8H2O. Erythrite and annabergite, chemical formula Ni3(AsO4)2•8H2O, or nickel arsenate form a complete series with the general formula (Co,Ni)3(AsO4)2•8H2O. Erythrite crystallizes in the monoclinic system and forms prismatic crystals. The color is crimson to pink and occurs as a secondary coating known as cobalt bloom on cobalt arsenide minerals. Well-formed crystals are rare, with most of the mineral manifesting in crusts or small reniform aggregates.","ru":"Эритри́н (англ. Erythrite от др.-греч. ἐρυθρός — красный), реже эритрит, а также ко́бальтовая о́хра (частично устар.) или кобальтовые цветы (устар.) — минерал класса арсенатов.","uk":"Еритри́н (кобальтові квіти) — мінерал класу арсенатів, водний арсенат кобальту шаруватої будови."},"fame":28,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-1213858","atoms":96,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[10.309,0.0,0.0],[0.0,13.492,0.0],[-1.198,0.0,4.616]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Co"},{"x":-1.198,"y":0.0,"z":4.616,"el":"Co"},{"x":0.0,"y":13.492,"z":0.0,"el":"Co"},{"x":-1.198,"y":13.492,"z":4.616,"el":"Co"},{"x":10.309,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Co"},{"x":9.112,"y":0.0,"z":4.616,"el":"Co"},{"x":10.309,"y":13.492,"z":0.0,"el":"Co"},{"x":9.112,"y":13.492,"z":4.616,"el":"Co"},{"x":5.155,"y":1.57,"z":0.0,"el":"Co"},{"x":3.957,"y":1.57,"z":4.616,"el":"Co"},{"x":